@startuml gsm-sourcer-contribution-lifecycle

' ============================================================
' VISUAL THEME
' ============================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #57606A
skinparam DefaultFontName "SansSerif"
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #57606A
  FontColor #24292F
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8C5
skinparam noteBorderColor #57606A

title GSM Sourcer - Contribution & SubjectIdentity lifecycle

note as Legend
  Two intertwined lifecycles:
  (1) **Contribution lifecycle** — every Contribution on every panel
      goes through Posted -> Considered -> (Winning | Superseded | Diagnosed).
  (2) **SubjectIdentity lifecycle** — a SubjectIdentity exists once
      its panel has at least one accepted Contribution; "convergence"
      is reached when no panel for it gains new Contributions and
      Validation passes.
end note

note as N_Contrib
  ============================
  CONTRIBUTION LIFECYCLE
  ============================
end note

[*] --> Posted : KS calls\nblackboard.post(panel, value)

state Posted {
  Posted : Engine attaches contributorKsId,\nderivedFrom, createdAt.
  Posted : cacheKey validated when\ndeterminism = NON_DETERMINISTIC.
}

Posted --> Considered : enters resolver pool\nfor (panel, identity, slot)

state Considered {
  Considered : ContributionResolver evaluates\nall current contributions.
}

Considered --> Winning : selected by resolver
Considered --> Losing : not selected\n(still kept for audit)
Considered --> Conflicted : resolver = failOnConflict\nand multiple contributions
Considered --> EscalatedToCheckpoint : resolver = userMediated\nand multiple contributions

Winning --> Superseded : new Contribution wins\nor user override
Winning --> [*] : Run ends with this winning

Losing --> Considered : new Contribution arrives\n-> resolver re-evaluates
Conflicted --> EscalatedToCheckpoint : Control routes to\nCheckpoint-A
EscalatedToCheckpoint --> Winning : user picks one\n(or appends override\nas a new Contribution)
EscalatedToCheckpoint --> Superseded : user drops this contribution

Posted --> Diagnosed : engine validation rejects\n(e.g. cacheKey missing)
Diagnosed --> [*]

note as N_SI
  ============================
  SUBJECTIDENTITY LIFECYCLE
  ============================
end note

state "SubjectIdentity lifecycle" as SI {

  [*] --> NotYetIdentified

  state "Identified\n(>= 1 SubjectIdentity contribution)" as Identified
  NotYetIdentified --> Identified : IdentificationKS\nposts SubjectIdentity\nfor identityKey K
  Identified --> Identified : ReconciliationKS posts\nadditional / merging\nSubjectIdentity contributions

  state "PanelsAccreting\n(other panels gain Contributions:\nArchetyping / Statement / Granularity /\nEvidence / Confidence)" as PanelsAccreting
  Identified --> PanelsAccreting : trigger predicates fire\nover Blackboard state

  state "Quiescent\n(no new Contributions for\nN consecutive Control iterations)" as Quiescent
  PanelsAccreting --> Quiescent : Control convergence\ndetector

  state "AwaitingCheckpointA" as CA
  Quiescent --> CA : if checkpoints.A\nenabled
  Quiescent --> ReadyForPipeline : if checkpoints.A\ndisabled

  state CA {
    state "Reviewing" as CA_Review
    state "Approved" as CA_Approved
    state "Override applied" as CA_Override
    state "Rejected" as CA_Rejected
    CA_Review --> CA_Approved : user: approve
    CA_Review --> CA_Override : user: append\nuser-mediated\nContribution
    CA_Review --> CA_Rejected : user: drop identity
  }

  CA_Approved --> ReadyForPipeline
  CA_Override --> PanelsAccreting : Control re-fires\ntriggers (cascade)
  CA_Rejected --> Dropped

  state Dropped <<end>>
  state ReadyForPipeline

  ReadyForPipeline --> Validating : Pipeline picks up\nresolved tuple

  state Validating
  Validating --> AwaitingCheckpointB : OK
  Validating --> PanelsAccreting : failed\n-> diagnostic + re-fire

  state AwaitingCheckpointB
  AwaitingCheckpointB --> Registering : approved
  AwaitingCheckpointB --> PanelsAccreting : override\n(cascade)
  AwaitingCheckpointB --> Dropped : rejected

  state Registering
  Registering --> [*] : DefMan DRAFT registered
}

note right of CA
  Checkpoints A and B are GOVERNANCE OVERLAYS,
  not part of the canonical Blackboard. They suspend
  the Run for user mediation. Override = append a new
  Contribution (with confidence = 1.0, contributorKsId
  = user) that supersedes the prior winner. Override-
  cascade: Control invalidates dependent resolved
  values across panels and re-fires triggers.
end note

@enduml
